  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The bullpen broke what the starter built. Landen Roupp gave them six innings on one earned run. Clean work. But Caleb Kilian and Matt Gage turned a 3-2 lead into a 5-3 loss in the ninth. Arizona didn't beat them. The Giants beat themselves in a single inning.",
    "what_this_means": "They had chances and left them there. Seven runners in scoring position, zero conversions. The sixth inning was critical. Two men on, two outs, nothing came of it. That's not close. That's careless. Roupp kept them within reach all night; the offense stayed quiet when it mattered most and the bullpen collapsed when it had to hold. This team doesn't lose by accident, but it's started losing like this more often. Good enough pitching, good enough at-bats, and then the moment arrives and they're not ready. Eight left on base says what happened.",
    "what_to_watch": "Merrill Kelly carries a 5.91 ERA into tonight's rematch. The Giants' offense found almost nothing yesterday; Kelly's numbers suggest they should find something today. Tyler Mahle goes for the Giants with more at stake than a division game. It's about whether they can close out a series or whether they're about to spiral.",
